No test in t/ reads the cpanfile, so a prerequisite that the code uses but that is missing in the cpanfile stays unnoticed. The missing https prerequisite of the cpanfile is exactly such a case.

Decide: a new t/cpanfile.t reads the cpanfile and checks every prerequisite that the code uses. /home/getty/dev/p5-www-vastai/t/cpanfile.t is the pattern to follow.

Commit 3424574: t/cpanfile.t reads the cpanfile and checks HTTP::Request, JSON::MaybeXS, LWP::UserAgent, LWP::Protocol::https, Moo, Safe::Isa and URI. Red proof: the test reads a file, not the behaviour, so it is not red against the old lib/; against the cpanfile before k4 it is red (LWP::Protocol::https missing). Suite: 17 files / 132 tests green (offline).

Commit 3c37958 (ersetzt 3424574, History neu geschrieben, Inhalt unveraendert): t/cpanfile.t liest das cpanfile und prueft HTTP::Request, JSON::MaybeXS, LWP::UserAgent, LWP::Protocol::https, Moo, Safe::Isa und URI. Suite: 17 Dateien / 135 Tests gruen (offline).
